<title>GERMANY: German Plettac maintains 1996 dividend.</title>
<headline>German Plettac maintains 1996 dividend.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>German scaffold-maker Plettac AG said on Monday that despite lower profits it would maintain its 1996 dividend at 11 marks per share.</p>
<p>The group said 1996 profits from ordinary activities fell to 99 million marks from 109 million on turnover up 20 percent at 977 million marks.</p>
<p>Plettac said that, including the electronic security products division recently taken over from Grundig, it was expecting 1997 group sales of 1.2 billion marks.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
